  "content": {
    "id": "p8-q12-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "12",
    "prompt": "Four congruent triangles make a square with side lengths equal to $c$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [
      {
        "id": "p8-q12-diagram",
        "role": "question",
        "format": "tikz",
        "code": "% mathsmap-diagram-colours {\"version\":1,\"kind\":\"geometry\",\"base\":[],\"semantic\":[{\"name\":\"shortLegBlue\",\"hex\":\"268CFF\",\"reason\":\"identifies the four congruent short legs\"},{\"name\":\"longLegOrange\",\"hex\":\"EF8B2C\",\"reason\":\"identifies the perpendicular long legs and their inner-square portions\"},{\"name\":\"outerSquareRed\",\"hex\":\"EF6068\",\"reason\":\"distinguishes the outer square whose side is c\"}],\"reference\":\"source page 8, p8-q12-diagram\"}\n\\begin{tikzpicture}[x=1cm,y=1cm,line cap=round,line join=round]\n\\special{dvisvgm:raw <metadata data-graph-strokes=\"1\"/>}\n\\definecolor{shortLegBlue}{HTML}{268CFF}\n\\definecolor{longLegOrange}{HTML}{EF8B2C}\n\\definecolor{outerSquareRed}{HTML}{EF6068}\n\\coordinate (I) at (0,2);\n\\coordinate (J) at (2,2);\n\\coordinate (K) at (2,0);\n\\coordinate (L) at (0,0);\n\\coordinate (T) at (0,3);\n\\coordinate (R) at (3,2);\n\\coordinate (B) at (2,-1);\n\\coordinate (W) at (-1,0);\n\\draw[outerSquareRed,line width=0.8pt,dashed] (T)--(R)--(B)--(W)--cycle;\n\\draw[longLegOrange,line width=0.8pt] (I)--(R) (J)--(B) (K)--(W) (L)--(T);\n\\draw[shortLegBlue,line width=0.8pt] (T)--(I) (R)--(J) (B)--(K) (W)--(L);\n\\path (T)--(I) node[midway,right,font=\\fontsize{10}{12}\\selectfont,text=black] {$a$};\n\\path (I)--(R) node[midway,above,font=\\fontsize{10}{12}\\selectfont,text=black] {$b$};\n\\path (T)--(R) node[midway,above,sloped,font=\\fontsize{10}{12}\\selectfont,text=black] {$c$};\n\\end{tikzpicture}",
        "src": null,
        "widthMm": 65,
        "alt": "Mathematical diagram",
        "overlayOf": null,
        "transparent": false,
        "axes": null,
        "spec": {
          "sourcePage": 8,
          "sourceRegion": "Question 12, figure beneath the shared stem",
          "description": "An unshaded tilted outer square encloses four congruent right triangles and an upright inner square. The upper triangle has a short vertical leg a, a full horizontal leg b and outer hypotenuse c. All four short legs remain blue, full long legs orange and the dashed outer boundary red.",
          "mathematics": "The outer vertices are (0,3), (3,2), (2,-1), (-1,0); the inner vertices are (0,2), (2,2), (2,0), (0,0). These illustrative coordinates construct four congruent right triangles without introducing printed numerical givens. Each triangle has perpendicular legs a and b and hypotenuse c; the inner square has side b-a.",
          "answerVisibility": "Only the supplied labels a, b and c are visible; no derived lengths, areas or theorem are printed."
